-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",342,{
[10913]="70016024\n1\tExamine the statue\tThe statue base is in the courtyard hall just to the south-east of Uxi. Uxi told you to examine the statue base so that you will be able to recognize its other pieces.\n2\tTalk to Uxi at the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tUxi is at the Chamber of the Cross-roads, north-west of the statue. You should return to Uxi for more instruction.\n",
[10914]="7001D0DA\n1\tDestroy catapults (total: 5)\tOrkish catapults can be found throughout northern Gathbúrz. Vatnar has asked you to destroy several Orkish catapults.\n2\tTalk to Vatnar in Thangúlhad\tVatnar is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz. You should return to Vatnar with tidings of your success.\n",
[10915]="7003FFDA\n1\tDefeat corsair looters (total: 4)\tThe windows should be saved.\n",
[10916]="70035993\n1\tTalk to Mossbeard\tMossbeard is standing at your side. Mossbeard wishes to tell you of what the trees of the Balewood have told him of Núrzum's origins.\n2\tTalk to Mossbeard\tMossbeard is standing at your side. Mossbeard's story has concluded and you should now speak with him before you set off to return to Barallas and the other Ents.\n",
[10917]="7005841B\n1\tDestroy sarrowstones in Malkorlash (total: 12)\tThe Malkorlash encampment is in the central north region of Elderslade. You should destroy the sarrowstones in the Malkorlash encampment.\n2\tTalk to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in the forge at Annâk-khurfu. You should talk to Mother Amma.\n",
[10918]="70001741\n1\tFind Elúr and speak with him\tElúr can be found at his encampment south of Esteldín, north of the waste-land that is Dol Dínen. You should find Elúr and hear out his concerns about what he's witnessed at Dol Dínen.\n2\tCollect Ongbúrz badges (total: 8)\tOngbúrz skirmishers can be found among the goblins who patrol the outskirts of the Orc-host in Dol Dínen, south-east of Esteldín. Elúr told you about the skirmishers of the Ongbúrz tribe, and has asked you to slay them in hopes that the army at Dol Dínen will be deterred.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have collected several Ongbúrz badges, indicating that the enemy force in Dol Dínen is stronger and more organized than any in the North Downs would wish.\n",
[10919]="7004BEA9\n1\tDefeat Shatúrro, the Spear\tShatúrro can be found in Fushaum Bal South. You should defeat Shatúrro.\n2\tTalk to the Khundolar Commander\tThe Khundolar Commander can be found at Fushaum Bal North. You should talk to the Khundolar Commander.\n",
[10920]="7004BEAF\n1\tDefeat Shatúrro's hunters (total: 4)\tShatúrro's hunters can be found in Fushaum Bal South. You should defeat any hunters under the command of Shatúrro.\n2\tTalk to the Khundolar Commander\tThe Khundolar Commander can be found at Fushaum Bal North. You should talk to the Khundolar Commander.\n",
[10921]="7000A16C\n1\tReturn to Uidon\030Collect Fragment of Ancient Armour (total: 12)\tAncient armour wreathes terrifying creatures within Barad Gúlaran. Collect these items and return them to Uidon at the encampment in the north-eastern area of Angmar. Uidon asked you to obtain samples of the armour worn by the defenders within Barad Gúlaran so he might learn a weakness to better defeat them. Make your way into Barad Gúlaran, with the assistance of others and collect the samples.\n",
[10922]="7003A5C5\n1\tTalk to Cúthing\tAn injured Cúthing approaches. Meregyth wants you to speak with Cúthing.\n2\tTalk to Meregyth\tMeregyth stands near the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch. You should speak with Meregyth concerning Cúthing's report.\n",
[10923]="700033CD\n1\tFind Mungo's stolen sheep\tMungo's prized ewe is being held captive in the goblin-camp in the north-east corner of the Greenfields. Mungo Burrows has asked you to fight your way into a goblin-camp and bring his stolen sheep safely outside. He suggested that you bring friends, or you may end up the goblins' next meal.\n2\tTalk to Mungo Burrows\tMungo Burrows is outside the goblin camp in the north-east corner of the Greenfields. Mungo is delighted that you brought his sheep safely from the camp of goblins who stole her and wants to speak with you at once.\n",
[10924]="700381C6\n1\tDestroy Orc targeting banners or banner carriers ([see journal]/20)\tOrcs are trying to plant targeting banners upon the Deeping wall to help guide the aim of their catapults. The Orcs must be dealt with and their banners torn down to avoid shells from consistently striking the wall. This will allow supplies to be delivered to the Hornburg from the siege towers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[10925]="7007179F\n1\tDefeat Adagím wood-trolls (total: 5)\030Collect bog-lurker carapaces (total: 6)\tBog-lurkers to the south-east of Laivárth seem to be resistant to the blight. Bring Tálbiral their shells for him to inspect. Be sure to defeat any wood-trolls you encounter in the area as well.\n2\tReturn to Tálbiral\tBring the gathered bog-lurker carapaces back to Tálbiral in Laivárth so that he can inspect them for signs of the blight.\n",
[10926]="70062F1D\n1\tSpeak with the emissary of Shelob's Brood\tYou may seek the blessing of Shelob's Brood. All you need do is renounce all other clans.\n",
[10927]="7005AAF0\n1\tTake down hobgoblin tents (total: 7)\030Clean up hobgoblin refuse (total: 7)\tDréri has asked you to take down the hobgoblin tents and clean up hobgoblin refuse in Fellgát.\n2\tSet up your packed tent\030Set up Kyrstig's packed tent\030Set up Molkha's packed tent\030Set up Klúso's packed tent\030Set up Hórin's packed tent\030Set up Dréri's packed tent\030Set up Náth's packed tent\tNow that the camp has been cleared, you should set up the packed tents. You should unpack and set up tents in Fellgát.\n3\tTalk to Dréri\tFellgát is now cleared of hobgoblin structures and ready for dwarf use. You should talk to Dréri.\n",
[10928]="7006AE13\n1\tTalk to Dabôr the Breaker within Hulzidâr, beneath the arena\tBeneath Dahâl Huliz, there is a small settlement in the catacombs that has been established by Rothog. He requested that you seek out Dabôr the Breaker to see how you might be of some assistance.\n",
[10929]="7003FDDE\n1\tSearch houses (total: 4)\tBandits may be hiding in some of the houses at the docks.\n",
[10930]="7003A5BF\n1\tCollect prepared food in the Mead Hall (total: 3)\tPrepared food can be found in the rear of the Mead Hall of Underharrow. Ellen Fremedon has asked that you set the tables with prepared food in the Mead Hall so that the refugees might feast before their journey.\n2\tSet tables in the Mead Hall at Underharrow (total: 8)\tTables can be found throughout the Mead Hall of Underharrow. You have gathered food and should now set tables in the Mead Hall for the refugees at Underharrow.\n3\tTalk to Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon can be found outside of the Mead Hall of Underharrow. You have set the tables and prepared a fine shelter for the refugees at Underharrow.\n",
[10931]="7006C534\n1\tCollect jackal hides from within Khûd Zagin ([see journal]/8)\030Collect scorpion chitin from the quarry in Khûd Zagin ([see journal]/8)\030Collect lizard frills from around Khûd Zagin ([see journal]/8)\tAshkab requires scorpion chitin, jackal hides, and lizard frills to help clothe and shelter the people of Jirush. He suggests the jackals can be found west in the waste-plains, scorpions in the quarry north-west of Jirush, and lizards to south-west of Jirush.\n2\tDeliver the jackal hides, scorpion chitin, and lizard frills to Ashkab in Jirush\tYou hunted the wildlife of Khûd Zagin for their hide, chitin, and leathery frills. You should deliver the items to Ashkab at his home in Jirush.\n",
[10932]="70062136\n1\tFill the trough outside of Hulfryn's home with hay\tBefore you go searching for Hulfryn's sheep, you should fill the trough outside his home with hay.\n2\tHulfryn's five sheep have fled their pen. You should find them around Herne and pet them to calm them down.\t\n3\tFind and pet sheep in Herne (4/5)\tHulfryn's five sheep have fled their pen. You should find them around Herne and pet them to calm them down.\n4\tTalk to Hulfryn\tThe fifth sheep remains missing. You should tell Hulfryn. His home is in the south-west corner of Herne.\n",
[10933]="70000CF1\n1\tDefeat wights near the place where the brothers placed the Cardolan treasure (total: 6)\tDead rise near a south facing wall among burial mounds of Men. The shade, in its cryptic way, asked you for assistance in ridding the place where he died of the fell barrow-wights.\n2\tTalk to the Wandering Shade in the northern Barrow-downs\tThe Wandering Shade is in the northern Barrow-downs. You found wights, risen from their graves, and defeated them at the pass leading to the southern Barrow-downs.\n",
[10934]="700375C4\n1\tTalk to Thane Ordlac to attend Reeve Fríthild's funeral\tThane Ordlac is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should speak with Thane Ordlac when you are prepared to attend Fríthild's funeral.\n2\tTalk to Thane Ordlac\tThane Ordlac is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should speak with Thane Ordlac regarding the funeral.\n",
[10935]="70069445\n1\tCraft a crate of shields for the Umbar Metalsmith's Guild\tThe recipe needed to complete this quest is available for purchase. Purchase the quest recipe from the guild leader. Pack a crate of shields for Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tDeliver a crate of shields to the Umbar Metalsmith's Guild Leader\tProvide the crate of shields to the Umbar Metalsmith's Guild Leader.\n",
[10936]="7006B10A\n1\tCraft a crate of shields for the Umbar Metalsmith's Guild\tThe recipe needed to complete this quest is available for purchase. Purchase the quest recipe from the guild leader. Pack a crate of shields for Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tDeliver a crate of shields to the Umbar Metalsmith's Guild Leader\tProvide the crate of shields to the Umbar Metalsmith's Guild Leader.\n",
[10937]="7006944A\n1\tComplete Umbar Metalsmith's Guild daily orders (total: 5)\tComplete requests from the Umbar Metalsmith's Guild. You can acquire these quests from the Umbar Metalsmith's Guild Leader in the Umbar Baharbêl craft guild hall.\n2\tCompleted\tYou completed many Umbar metalsmith requests.\n",
[10938]="70065997\n1\tTalk to Lastriel\tMaldor has asked you to check on the guards stationed at the front gate. Go to the front gate of Ost Anglebed.\n2\tTalk to Maldor\tLastriel has asked you to return the sergeant with the promise that she will report in soon Talk to Maldor in Ost Anglebed.\n",
[10939]="7005F6B8\n1\tTide-pools can be found at Skelstrand in Gloomingtarn. Orti has asked you to pan the tide-pools of Skelstrand for the source of a mysterious shimmer he spied from Watchers' Roost. You should pan the tide-pools of Skelstrand.\t\n2\tTalk to Orti\tOrti can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. Despite seeing the shimmers Orti described, panning the waters of Durthuzâram has not yielded anything. You should return to Orti.\n",
[10940]="70069072\n1\tDefeat drowned wights (total: 6)\030Defeat blight-callers (total: 8)\030Defeat brine-drinkers (total: 2)\030Rescue captive sailors (total: 3)\030Find and rescue noblewoman\tA prominent Umbari noble has vanished during a routine trip to the Shedax Khîn in the Shield Isles, near an isle it's rumoured the dead walk freely. Investigate and rescue any trapped sailors.\n2\tDefeat Rûpharo the Rancorous\tFind and defeat Rûpharo the Rancorous!\n3\tFind the Scout\t\n",
[10941]="7000BFE2\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Mathom Society.\n",
[10942]="7000BFE3\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Mathom Society.\n",
[10943]="7000BFE4\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Mathom Society.\n",
[10944]="7000BFE5\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred with the Mathom Society.\n",
})
